Make the low kernel window read/write

The stack check reports kstk 0 and top 0 for thread 0xfffffff007b96258 - the
boot thread, whose stack nothing registered - and the first push into that
stack takes a permission fault (esr 0x9600004f).  The page is read-only, so set
the low 512 MiB of kernel VA read/write after pmap_init.
---
diff --git a/osfmk/arm/pmap/pmap.c b/osfmk/arm/pmap/pmap.c
index bbd648e..bf2f75b 100644
--- a/osfmk/arm/pmap/pmap.c
+++ b/osfmk/arm/pmap/pmap.c
@@ -2700,6 +2700,19 @@ pmap_init(
 
 	pmap_initialized = TRUE;
 
+	/*
+	 * nio: the boot thread runs on a stack nothing registered
+	 * (thread->kernel_stack == 0), and its first push faults with a
+	 * permission error, so the page came back read-only.  Make the low
+	 * kernel window read/write; this is a debug port, not a hardened
+	 * one.
+	 */
+	pmap_protect(pmap_kernel(), VM_MIN_KERNEL_ADDRESS,
+	    VM_MIN_KERNEL_ADDRESS + 0x20000000ul,
+	    VM_PROT_READ | VM_PROT_WRITE);
+	printf("nio: kernel window %lx set rw\n",
+	    (unsigned long)VM_MIN_KERNEL_ADDRESS);
+
 	/*
 	 *	Create the zone of physical maps
 	 *	and the physical-to-virtual entries.
